[00:00.00]There is a flower within my heart,
[00:04.00]Daisy, Daisy!
[00:08.00]Planted one day by a glancing dart,
[00:12.00]Planted by Daisy Bell!
[00:16.00]Whether she loves me or loves me not,
[00:20.00]Sometimes it's hard to tell;
[00:24.00]Yet I am longing to share the lot
[00:28.00]Of beautiful Daisy Bell!
[00:32.00]Daisy, Daisy, give me your answer, do!
[00:36.00]I'm half crazy, all for the love of you!
[00:40.00]It won't be a stylish marriage,
[00:44.00]I can't afford a carriage,
[00:48.00]But you'll look sweet upon the seat
[00:52.00]Of a bicycle built for two!
[00:56.00]We will go "tandem" as man and wife,
[01:00.00]Daisy, Daisy!
[01:04.00]"Ped'ling" away down the road of life,
[01:08.00]I and my Daisy Bell!
[01:12.00]When the road's dark we can both despise
[01:16.00]P'licemen and "lamps" as well;
[01:20.00]There are "bright lights" in the dazzling eyes
[01:24.00]Of beautiful Daisy Bell!